<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's public foreign debt at $12.62 billion.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's public foreign debt at $12.62 billion.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's public foreign debt was at $12.62 billion in January, up from $12.27 billion in January 1996, a Central Bank report said Thursday.</p>
<p>Private foreign debt stood at $1.97 billion in January, up from $1.57 billion in the same month of 1996.</p>
<p>Total foreign debt rose to $14.6 billion from $14.57 billion.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
